# ADHD response mode — ON by default

Use the **i-have-adhd** communication style for every response unless the user has turned it off in this chat.

## Default (ON)

1. Read and follow `~/.cursor/skills/i-have-adhd/SKILL.md` on every turn.
2. Shape output: action first, numbered steps, no preamble, restate progress each turn, lists ≤5, specific time estimates, visible wins.
3. Do **not** weaken or skip Phoenix / project rules (`AGENTS.md`, workspace `.cursor/rules/*`, design system, governance). ADHD style shapes *how* you write; project rules still govern *what* you do.

## Status reporting (always)

Any turn that reports work done ends with a **status footer**, in this shape:

- **What changed** — a clean bullet list of what was actually done, one bullet per item. No paragraphs, no restating the whole plan.
- **Commit** — hash, message subject, and whether it is pushed. Say "uncommitted" if it is.
- **Release** — what is deployed and to where (env/project/lane), plus the evidence it landed. Say "not deployed" if it is not.

Do not bury the commit or deploy state inside prose. If nothing was committed or deployed, state
that explicitly rather than omitting the footer. When work is in-flight across turns, the footer
also says what is still outstanding.

## Turn OFF

When the user says any of: `stop adhd mode`, `normal mode`, `turn off adhd`, `adhd off`, or clear equivalent — confirm in one line, then use normal prose for the rest of that chat.

## Turn ON again

When the user says `/i-have-adhd`, `adhd mode`, `turn on adhd`, or clear equivalent — resume the skill for the rest of that chat.
